{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++0x code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++0x code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <limits>\n#include <cstdint>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i128 = __int128_t;\n\ni128 gcd(i128 a, i128 b) {\n    while (b) {\n        a %= b;\n        swap(a, b);\n    }\n    return a;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n\n    long long best_num = 0, best_den = 1;\n    double min_err = numeric_limits<double>::infinity();\n\n    for (long long d = 1; d <= n; ++d) {\n        long long num1 = 0;\n        long long lo = 0, hi = 100000;\n        while (lo <= hi) {\n            long long mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n            if (static_cast<i128>(mid) * y <= static_cast<i128>(x) * d) {\n                num1 = mid;\n                lo = mid + 1;\n            } else {\n                hi = mid - 1;\n            }\n        }\n\n        long long num2 = 0;\n        lo = 0, hi = 100000;\n        while (lo <= hi) {\n            long long mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n            if (static_cast<i128>(mid) * y < static_cast<i128>(x) * d) {\n                lo = mid + 1;\n            } else {\n                num2 = mid;\n                hi = mid - 1;\n            }\n        }\n\n        double err1 = fabs(static_cast<double>(num1) / d - static_cast<double>(x) / y);\n        double err2 = fabs(static_cast<double>(num2) / d - static_cast<double>(x) / y);\n\n        long long chosen_num = num1;\n        long long chosen_den = d;\n        double chosen_err = err1;\n\n        if (err2 < err1 - 1e-15) {\n            chosen_num = num2;\n            chosen_den = d;\n            chosen_err = err2;\n        }\n\n        long long g = gcd(chosen_num, chosen_den);\n        chosen_num /= g;\n        chosen_den /= g;\n\n        if (chosen_err < min_err) {\n            best_num = chosen_num;\n            best_den = chosen_den;\n            min_err = chosen_err;\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << best_num << \"/\" << best_den << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport math\nimport sys\n\ndef gcd(a, b):\n    while b:\n        a %= b\n        a, b = b, a\n    return a\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    x = int(data[0])\n    y = int(data[1])\n    n = int(data[2])\n    \n    best_num = 0\n    best_den = 1\n    min_err = float('inf')\n    \n    for d in range(1, n + 1):\n        # Binary search for num1: largest num such that num * y <= x * d\n        lo, hi = 0, 100000\n        num1 = 0\n        while lo <= hi:\n            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n            if mid * y <= x * d:\n                num1 = mid\n                lo = mid + 1\n            else:\n                hi = mid - 1\n        \n        # Binary search for num2: smallest num such that num * y >= x * d\n        lo, hi = 0, 100000\n        num2 = 0\n        while lo <= hi:\n            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n            if mid * y >= x * d:\n                num2 = mid\n                hi = mid - 1\n            else:\n                lo = mid + 1\n        \n   